{
  "editable": true,
  "panels": [
    {
      "collapsed": false,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0
      },
      "id": 1,
      "panels": [],
      "title": "Position integrity",
      "type": "row"
    },
    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "carry-prometheus"
      },
      "description": "acc_position{type=remote} minus {type=local}. 'local' is the engine's own fill-derived tally; 'remote' is what the venue reports. They are independent paths, so a persistent gap is the ONLY evidence available that fills have been missed.\n\nEMPTY DOES NOT MEAN AGREEMENT. The 'local' series is created inside the fill handler (Account.cs), so it does not exist at all between a restart and the first fill - and a book sitting at target may not fill for hours. A blank panel means there is nothing to compare yet. Check 'Position by symbol' beside this one: if it shows only type=remote, that is why.\n\nOnce both exist, a persistent gap is serious: the strategy sizes from the local number, so a stale one means it trades against a position that does not exist. That is how a dropped feed let the same order go out 25 times against a position reading 0.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "spanNulls": true
          },
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": 1e-06
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 9,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 1
      },
      "id": 2,
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "acc_position{setup=\"$setup\", host=~\"$host\", symbol=~\"$symbol\", type=\"remote\"} - on(instance, account, symbol) acc_position{setup=\"$setup\", host=~\"$host\", symbol=~\"$symbol\", type=\"local\"}",
          "legendFormat": "{{symbol}}",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "title": "Position drift: engine vs venue (needs a fill first)",
      "type": "timeseries"
    },
    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "carry-prometheus"
      },
      "description": "Repeated across every symbol the account touches, from label_values - so a new instrument appears without a dashboard edit.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "spanNulls": true
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 9,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 1
      },
      "id": 3,
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "acc_position{setup=\"$setup\", host=~\"$host\", symbol=~\"$symbol\"}",
          "legendFormat": "{{symbol}} ({{type}})",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "title": "Position by symbol",
      "type": "timeseries"
    },
    {
      "collapsed": false,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 10
      },
      "id": 10,
      "panels": [],
      "title": "Liveness",
      "type": "row"
    },
    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "carry-prometheus"
      },
      "description": "Zero on a connector that should be live means the venue link is dead even though the process is up. Every incident worth alerting on this session was silent in exactly this way.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "spanNulls": true
          },
          "unit": "cps"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 11
      },
      "id": 11,
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "sum(rate(connector_messages{setup=\"$setup\", host=~\"$host\"}[$__rate_interval])) by (connector)",
          "legendFormat": "{{connector}}",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "title": "Connector message rate",
      "type": "timeseries"
    },
    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "carry-prometheus"
      },
      "description": "binance_timeshift. recvWindow is spent on one-way latency PLUS this offset, so drift here is the leading indicator for -1021 'Timestamp outside recvWindow' - which presents as a strategy that silently never fills, not as a clock problem.\n\nThis metric already existed and was never watched; a 217ms drift from an unsynced clock broke every order until it was found by hand.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "spanNulls": true
          },
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "orange",
                "value": 50
              },
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": 200
              }
            ]
          },
          "unit": "ms"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 11
      },
      "id": 12,
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "binance_timeshift{setup=\"$setup\", host=~\"$host\"}",
          "legendFormat": "{{host}}",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "title": "Clock offset vs venue (ms)",
      "type": "timeseries"
    },
    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "carry-prometheus"
      },
      "description": "order_delay by type. A rising tail here alongside rejections usually means the place-staleness guard is firing rather than the venue refusing.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "spanNulls": true
          },
          "unit": "ms"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 19
      },
      "id": 13,
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.5, sum(rate(order_delay_bucket{setup=\"$setup\", host=~\"$host\"}[$__rate_interval])) by (le, type))",
          "legendFormat": "p50 {{type}}",
          "refId": "A"
        },
        {
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.95, sum(rate(order_delay_bucket{setup=\"$setup\", host=~\"$host\"}[$__rate_interval])) by (le, type))",
          "legendFormat": "p95 {{type}}",
          "refId": "B"
        }
      ],
      "title": "Order delay",
      "type": "timeseries"
    },
    {
      "type": "row",
      "id": 19,
      "title": "Market data quality",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 27
      },
      "collapsed": false,
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "type": "histogram",
      "id": 20,
      "title": "Quotes drift histogram — $venue",
      "description": "Distribution of quote arrival drift over the window, as the OKX colo dashboard shows it. Shape is the point: a tight cluster is a healthy feed, a long right tail means quotes arrive late in bursts and the strategy prices off stale data some of the time.\n\nBINANCE IS STRUCTURALLY ZERO HERE - it is not a latency result. Drift is LocalTimestamp minus RemoteTimestamp, and the Binance spot connector sets both to the same value because the @bookTicker stream carries no exchange event time to subtract. Hyperliquid's BBO does carry one, so its drift is real. Compare HL against itself over time; do not compare the two venues.\n\nBuckets hold drift RELATIVE to the running minimum for the venue, so read this as spread. The median panel adds the minimum back.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "carry-prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 9,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 28
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "custom": {
            "fillOpacity": 80,
            "gradientMode": "none",
            "lineWidth": 1,
            "stacking": {
              "group": "A",
              "mode": "none"
            }
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "calcs": [],
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "showLegend": true
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "single",
          "sort": "none"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "editorMode": "code",
          "format": "heatmap",
          "range": true,
          "legendFormat": "__auto",
          "expr": "sum by (le) (increase(md_${venue}_quotes_drift_bucket{setup=\"$setup\", host=~\"$host\"}[5m]))"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "id": 21,
      "title": "Quotes drift median — $venue",
      "description": "Median quote drift, with the venue's minimum added back so this is absolute rather than relative to the floor.\n\nHyperliquid sits around 151 ms from Tokyo; Binance reads 0 because its spot quotes carry no exchange timestamp for the engine to compare against, not because they arrive instantly. Only HL's line carries information here.\n\nWhat matters is the line MOVING. A rising median means quotes are arriving later, which shows up in trading as hedging against a market that has already moved.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "carry-prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 9,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 28
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "ms",
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "spanNulls": true
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "calcs": [],
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "showLegend": true
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "single",
          "sort": "none"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "editorMode": "code",
          "range": true,
          "legendFormat": "$venue median",
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.5, sum(rate(md_${venue}_quotes_drift_bucket{setup=\"$setup\", host=~\"$host\"}[5m])) by (le)) + avg(md_${venue}_quotes_drift_min{setup=\"$setup\", host=~\"$host\"})"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "refresh": "30s",
  "schemaVersion": 39,
  "tags": [
    "carry",
    "robot"
  ],
